# Medora UI Standards Enforcement

When building UI in `apps/web`:

## MUST FOLLOW

- `docs/ui/medora-ui-standards.md`
- `apps/web/src/components/medora-card/` tokens (`medoraCardTokens.ts`) and components (`MedoraCard`, etc.)

Complements `.cursor/rules/medora-card-system.mdc` (clinical list rows / worklist primitives).

## DO NOT

- Introduce new card shells for clinical list rows outside `MedoraCard` (see medora-card-system rule).
- Introduce ad hoc palettes outside the documented system (shell border `#e2e8f0`, canvas `#f8fafc`, tokens in `medoraCardTokens.ts`).
- Mix inconsistent spacing or radius (prefer shell `radius: 16`, inner inputs ~10–12, badges pill `9999` per existing components).

## ALWAYS

- Use `MedoraCard` (+ `MedoraCardInner`, etc.) for clinical list rows where the worklist pattern applies.
- Use `MEDORA_CARD_SHELL` (or components that apply it) for simple panels / section shells.
- Use `MedoraCardRoomBlock` for room/location emphasis in card rows.
- Use `MedoraCardBadge` with `preset` or `soft` (`PriorityBadgeSoft` from tokens) before inventing new badge styles.

## SAFE RULE

If unsure → STOP and ask.
